  "title": "S1a: canonical skill registry (P1/P2 states, P22 versions by content hash, P32 provenance fields) built from skills/**/SKILL.md, `orchestrator skills` CLI, and the P0 inventory doc",
  "spec": "Program brief .orchestrator/roadmap-skills.md P0, P1, P2, P22, P32 (P37 stage 1). Facts (Planner grep, provenance repo): 12 skills under skills/<role>/<name>/SKILL.md with YAML frontmatter (name, description; some carry scripts/ and references/); 11 are symlinked into .claude/skills so every Claude worker sees their descriptions; Codex executors load implement-spec through AGENTS.md; worker prompts do not name skills; no registry, telemetry or per-skill tests exist except tests/test_memory_skill.py; task classes come from attribution.task_class (security, architectural, debugging, mechanical, unfamiliar, or explicit constraints.task_class); workflow strategies are strategy.STRATEGIES.\nDo:\n1. orchestrator/skills_registry.py (new). `SkillRecord` dataclass with: id (f\"{role}/{name}\" from the directory path), version (12-hex sha256 of the SKILL.md body + scripts/ + references/ contents, i.e. a content hash; the same value is content_hash), name, description, provenance (\"builtin\" for skills/ in this repo; \"repository\", \"learned\", \"external\" reserved), trust (\"trusted\" | \"untrusted\"), state (one of STATES = discovered, quarantined, testing, shadow, active, demoted, disabled), roles (from the directory: planner/scout/review/triage/executor; \"review\" also serves spec_review and challenge; explicit override via an optional frontmatter key `roles:`), task_classes (frontmatter `task_classes:` or [\"*\"]), triggers (frontmatter `triggers:` list; default: keywords parsed from the description's \"Use when ...\" / \"Use for ...\" clause, lower-cased, \u22654 chars), tools (frontmatter `allowed-tools`/`tools:` plus every script under scripts/ as \"script:<path>\"), context_requirements (frontmatter `requires_context:` or []; P26 placeholder), output_contract (frontmatter `output:` or the text after \"Finish with\" / \"Output\" in the body, \u2264300 chars), est_tokens_l0 (description chars//4), est_tokens_l1 (trigger+objective+output chars//4 when present), est_tokens_l2 (full body chars//4), security_class (frontmatter `security:` or \"internal\"), repo_scope (\"orchestrator\" default; frontmatter `repo:`), validation ({\"tests\": [test module paths that mention the skill dir], \"status\": \"untested\"|\"tested\"}), promotion_state (mirror of state for the promotion module), created_at/updated_at (git log of the SKILL.md path; fall back to mtime), source (path).\n2. Registry store: `.orchestrator/skills/registry.json` (under STATE) with {\"version\": 1, \"synced_at\", \"skills\": {id: record}} plus a per-skill state override file `.orchestrator/skills/state.json` {id: {\"state\", \"trust\", \"since\", \"reason\", \"history\": [...]}} so lifecycle transitions are observable and reversible (P2): `transition(id, new_state, reason)` validates against ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS (discovered\u2192quarantined/testing/disabled; quarantined\u2192testing/disabled; testing\u2192shadow/disabled/quarantined; shadow\u2192active/testing/disabled; active\u2192demoted/disabled/shadow; demoted\u2192shadow/testing/disabled; disabled\u2192discovered/testing) and appends to history; `rollback(id)` restores the previous state. Builtin skills start in state \"active\" and trust \"trusted\" (explicit, recorded in state.json with reason \"builtin baseline 2026-09-22\"), never inferred from provenance at runtime: registry.state(id) reads state.json first.\n3. `sync(root=STATE, skills_dir=REPO/skills)` rebuilds records from disk, keeps state.json entries, marks skills whose content hash changed as version bumps (history entry \"content changed: old\u2192new\"; state unchanged for builtins, \"testing\" for anything not trusted), and marks missing skills \"disabled\" with reason \"source removed\".\n4. CLI: `orchestrator skills sync|list|show <id>|transition <id> <state> --reason|rollback <id>` (list prints id, state, trust, roles, est tokens l0/l2, version; --json). Exit non-zero on an invalid transition.\n5. docs/skill-intelligence/00-audit.md: the P0 inventory table (one row per skill: id, roles, purpose, trigger, tokens l0/l2, tools, output contract, repo specificity, always exposed?, dynamic?, tests, provenance) and the exposure facts above; docs/skill-intelligence/01-registry.md (\u226460 lines): the record schema, the state machine, the CLI, revert path (delete .orchestrator/skills/*.json and re-sync; nothing else changes).\nConstraints: read-only with respect to skills/ and .claude/skills (no compaction, no symlink changes: that is S2/S5); no behaviour change for any worker. Never quote double-brace placeholder tokens literally.\nTests (unittest, `import _harness` first): tests/test_skills_registry.py::test_sync_builds_twelve_builtin_records_with_content_hashes, ::test_triggers_parsed_from_use_when_clause, ::test_transition_validates_and_records_history, ::test_rollback_restores_previous_state, ::test_state_override_beats_provenance (a builtin marked disabled in state.json reports disabled), ::test_sync_marks_missing_skill_disabled_and_version_bump_on_content_change, ::test_cli_list_and_invalid_transition_exit_code.\nDo not ask questions; decide and note decisions in the result.",
